(BUF-06: fixed buffers do not grow - writes past capacity are rejected/truncated, not silently expanded.)
(expected output:
write past capacity errored
4
8
ABCD
)
a buffer called fx is 8 bytes in size.
append "ABCD" to fx.
Set byte 100 of fx to 9.
On error print "write past capacity errored".
print fx's size.
print fx's capacity.
print fx.
